  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FAME Dissemination Workshop</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FAME project is finalized in February 2022. One of the conclusions of the project is that 17% of the total extension of sand-dunes in the provinces of Ben Tre and Tra Vinh is suitable to implement Aquifer Storage and Recovery (ASR) systems. Several stakeholders have manifested their interest in the pilot and in discussing the results of FAME and the potential to include it in future programs and projects being developed in the region. With the objective to leverage on relations built during the project, and building on the already started conversations online, the project partners consider that a live meeting in the right context, the Vietnam International Water Week, can yield fruitful conversations and help the project partners advance towards the objective of following up and branching out the outcomes of FAME. Therefore, a dissemination workshop is organised to disseminate the findings of FAME, interact with stakeholders and discuss potential for scaling up ASR in the Mekong Delta.</narrative>
  </description>
